==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Li'l Zyclone]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Zapy]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Bring a Cat Cannon Recharge UP [[Cat Combo]] in order to unburrow every Li'l Zyclone when they arrive.

Farm up the Doge Darks at the beginning of the stage with [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for cash, then start sending out [[Talents|Talented]] [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cats]] to take care of the Zombies. [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] the initial Li'l Zyclone and use him as a stepping stone to snipe other incoming Zombies, since it deals basically no damage. Send out any other attackers you might have at this point like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], since you'll need all the DPS you can to kill the giant crowd of enemies alongside Zapy.

With [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]] as additional meatshields, the enemies will hardly be able to push onto your base. So once Zapy dies, cleanup should be a simple process.

